kind check-if
title Check if a terminal uses a look.
intro The Looks tab lists the looks of the draft. Beside the highlighted look, vtium-config says which terminals use it. Looking changes nothing.
see looks/make-a-look-and-use-it-on-the-console

file etc/vtium.conf
    version = 1
    font-name = unifont
    [look big]
    font-name = mono
    font-size = 24
    [look small]
    font-name = mono
    [head console]
    vt = 5
    look = big
file etc/batch.conf
    ROOT/fonts/mono.bdf
font fonts/mono.bdf 8x16
frit mono
    source=bdf:ROOT/fonts/mono.bdf

1. Go to the Looks tab.
2. Highlight big.
at big is highlighted
check screen shows "Terminal console uses it"
3. Highlight small.
at small is highlighted
check screen shows "No terminal uses it"
